        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ac59a83b-5cff-5c50-84be-349bce3bfa82",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Sikoryak, Samuel Beckett, Bob Kane, Daria Morgendorffer\n- Works and Series: Masterpiece Comics, Crime and Punishment, Dostoyevsky Comics, Waiting for Godot, Waiting to Go, Beavis and Butt-Head, Daria, Carousel\n- Roles and Concepts: American artist, comic adaptations, multimedia comics slide show, fictional character\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Sikoryak was born in 1964 and is an American artist whose work is usually signed R. Sikoryak.\n- Robert Sikoryak specializes in making comic adaptations of literary classics.\n- Under the series title Masterpiece Comics, Robert Sikoryak adapted Crime and Punishment in a Bob Kane-era Batman style as Dostoyevsky Comics, starring Raskol.\n- Under the series title Masterpiece Comics, Robert Sikoryak mixed Waiting for Godot with Beavis and Butt-Head to create Waiting to Go.\n- Waiting for Godot is a play by Samuel Beckett in which Vladimir and Estragon wait for someone named Godot, who never arrives, while they talk and encounter three other characters.\n- Carousel is a long-running multimedia comics slide show hosted by cartoonist Robert Sikoryak that has been presented in venues in the United States and Canada since 1997.\n- Daria Morgendorffer is a fictional character from MTV's animated series Beavis and Butt-Head and its spin-off Daria.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "41a04152-985d-5582-8cdb-7afb6dee7b27",
        "text": "Page: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Robert Sikoryak (born 1964) is an American artist whose work is usually signed R. Sikoryak.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: He specializes in making comic adaptations of literature classics.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Under the series title \"Masterpiece Comics\", these include \"Crime and Punishment\" rendered in Bob Kane–era Batman style, becoming \"Dostoyevsky Comics\", starring Raskol; and \"Waiting for Godot\" mixed with \"Beavis and Butt-Head\", becoming \"Waiting to Go\".\nPage: Waiting for Godot. Sentence: Waiting for Godot ( ) is a play by Samuel Beckett, in which two characters, Vladimir and Estragon, wait for the arrival of someone named Godot who never arrives, and while waiting they engage in a variety of discussions and encounter three other characters.\nPage: Carousel (comics). Sentence: Carousel is a long-running multimedia comics slide show hosted by cartoonist Robert Sikoryak (\"Masterpiece Comics\") that has been presented in various venues in the United States and Canada since 1997.\nPage: Daria Morgendorffer. Sentence: Daria Morgendorffer is a fictional character from MTV's animated series \"Beavis and Butt-Head\" and its spin-off \"Daria\".",
